    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "$x^3=71$. What is $(-x)^3$? Explain how you know.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$-71$, since $(-x)^3=-x^3$.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}(-x)^3&=(-x)\\times(-x)\\times(-x)\\\\(-x)^3&=-x^3\\\\(-x)^3&=-71\\end{align*}$$\nCubing the opposite number gives the opposite result.",
